<node id="iOS">
  <data key="d0">iOS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">iOS is a mobile operating system used by devices compatible with the CMF Watch app for the Watch Pro.&lt;SEP&gt;iOS is an operating system used by Apple mobile devices, which provides a platform for using apps including the Nothing X App.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-852b3a0efad903b6a432ebd5e7a404af</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597424</data>
</node>
<node id="Ear (open)">
  <data key="d0">Ear (open)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ear (open) are innovative wireless earbuds developed by Nothing, known for their unique ear-hook design and functionality. These earbuds offer gesture controls that allow users to manage functions like volume and noise cancellation, contingent upon device compatibility, although they do not support active noise cancellation (ANC). Featuring Bluetooth 5.3, they support Google Fast Pair, Microsoft Swift Pair, and Dual Connection capabilities, allowing seamless connectivity and automatic reconnection to the last paired device under specific conditions. Ear (open) are also equipped with IP54 water and dust resistance, custom EQ settings, and are designed to provide stability during outdoor activities. Compatible with Android 5.1 and above and iOS 13 and higher, they ensure wide usability across various devices. Recognized for their sound quality through user experiences, these earbuds can be managed using apps like the Nothing X App for enhanced control and personalization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ea28975423f6227a8330d76c202878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1887c3e753e5f27cc1105a32465893f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4524a05ac17de1be9923e9a9dc9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443862ed6a46e95ac18dbc4e38f2090</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597427</data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE)">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) is a wireless communication protocol used by the Nothing X App to connect with devices while conserving power, though communication is paused during calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597427</data>
</node>
<node id="Android">
  <data key="d0">Android</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Android is a widely used mobile operating system referenced in various contexts for app management and device connectivity. It is utilized by devices compatible with applications such as the Nothing X App, which manages device connections and requires specific permission settings to function effectively. Additionally, Android supports the CMF Watch app for the Watch Pro and is compatible with the Ear (stick) through Bluetooth integration, with version 5.0+ facilitating this connection. This operating system is further mentioned in scenarios related to confirming connections between devices, such as the Nothing Phone, and is integral to data transfer processes to this specific phone. Android serves as the primary operating system across a multitude of smartphones, supporting a range of applications and hardware functionalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-852b3a0efad903b6a432ebd5e7a404af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-136bde614c09969c0d7fb82cc253fd47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e6bb17059b6ce78b33dddb496db9d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d82ee9e80b9a4011cc5dfdad909fc2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597431</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing Ear">
  <data key="d0">Nothing Ear</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing Ear is a line of advanced wireless earbuds produced by Nothing Technology Limited, designed to integrate seamlessly with the Nothing Phone and other mobile devices. These earbuds boast a variety of cutting-edge audio technologies, including Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) and Dual Connection capabilities, allowing users to pair them with multiple devices simultaneously, up to eight connections. Bluetooth 5.3 support ensures efficient connectivity, while features like wireless and fast charging add to their convenience. The earbuds stand out with specific audio settings such as AAC mode to optimize battery life, custom EQ settings for tailored sound experiences, and Fast Pair connectivity for effortless pairing. Furthermore, the Nothing Ear can be managed through apps like the Nothing X App, enhancing user control over their listening experience. This product line showcases Nothing's commitment to delivering premium, versatile audio devices that cater to modern technological needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-762fda66ccc0b9dd4cae96c4b09a2422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01cde718609da4920ebfa164616b8d87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d629090523155bf0dd12f9021e8a28a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b8eb92f55e1f3c041c691be7b6dbda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124df9689f92596c4fbc5e0e680893f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9ca0a66c298c31fec04cbfc30d7b98c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1d82ee9e80b9a4011cc5dfdad909fc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597436</data>
</node>
