<node id="SIM Card">
  <data key="d0">SIM Card</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A SIM Card, or Subscriber Identification Module, is a critical component used in mobile devices, including smartphones such as the Nothing Phone, for network connectivity and cellular services. It is a removable, portable smart card designed to store user data and network authorization information, such as the phone number and carrier details, enabling the device to access various wireless services. SIM cards are essential for connecting mobile devices to cellular networks, supporting data and call functions, and facilitating network connectivity during the setup of new phones. They play a crucial role in managing communication functions and can be tested in different devices to address internet speed issues. SIM cards are often involved in the data transfer process and are necessary for network connectivity and phone operation. The Nothing Phone supports dual SIM capabilities, allowing the user flexibility in network connectivity, including dual 4G modes. Overall, SIM cards are indispensable for accessing mobile network information and managing data use and connectivity for seamless mobile communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecf49d9e86fc2b3fbfb0f065b82e03e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcacac32b6b6cffea40cb0a17d301d61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff9ab0e6b0a19cc3df9b2e42e60f607f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3de9a6eca983da6478af176236f5152b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6165e1e8378c1118b98626013d6262b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e6bb17059b6ce78b33dddb496db9d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d37b7781a21f9ace596c3bcb0cbfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7e41b65ef7bcc80c8f1decc9bf2928</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597451</data>
</node>
<node id="Browser">
  <data key="d0">Browser</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Browser is a software application used to access information on the World Wide Web.&lt;SEP&gt;A browser is a software application used to access and navigate the internet, offering features like clearing browsing data.&lt;SEP&gt;Browser is a device application that allows users to access internet sites and manage their browsing history and data.&lt;SEP&gt;The browser is an application type that might freeze and has specific instructions for troubleshooting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06e37afdf610d89a09df8901349a725e</data>
