<node id="Network Connection">
  <data key="d0">Network Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Network Connection denotes the linking of devices to the internet via WiFi or mobile data to enable app functionality and updates.&lt;SEP&gt;Network connection failures during a call can be caused by congestion, SIM card issues, or network conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-258395120725348800696992422fd798</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597474</data>
</node>
<node id="WiFi">
  <data key="d0">WiFi</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">WiFi is a versatile wireless networking technology that enables devices to connect to the internet or communicate with one another within a specific area. This technology is based on the IEEE 802.11 standards and plays a crucial role in wireless local area networking. WiFi uses radio waves to facilitate high-speed internet and network connections, making it essential for setting up and transferring data between devices, such as phones. It is also commonly referenced in airplane mode settings, demonstrating its ubiquity in modern electronic devices. Additionally, WiFi is a key technology utilized by devices like the Nothing Phone to establish internet connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff9ab0e6b0a19cc3df9b2e42e60f607f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3de9a6eca983da6478af176236f5152b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8238a048f616eaf02f92d0455ae0f39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59d089d6dd16ac59cfa0d577b293a12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abefe8b5c23aeae06eaa603651797d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7e41b65ef7bcc80c8f1decc9bf2928</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597480</data>
</node>
<node id="Developer Options">
  <data key="d0">Developer Options</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Developer Options are settings in a device's system that allow advanced configurations, including USB debugging.&lt;SEP&gt;Developer Options is a menu in Android devices that provides additional features for developers and advanced users to customize and troubleshoot the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Developer Options is a section in Android settings allowing advanced configuration and features for developers, like USB Debugging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fec2c3e80ab69404ff0b23b014c07483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9fb365d0322c82fb6ff52dc4a7925f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597480</data>
</node>
<node id="App Cache">
  <data key="d0">App Cache</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">App Cache refers to the temporary storage used by apps to store frequently accessed data for quick retrieval, which can be cleared to resolve issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-946e2c39d383e3255fe1b3a1508733e8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597480</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF Buds Pro 2">
  <data key="d0">CMF Buds Pro 2</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">The CMF Buds Pro 2 are advanced wireless earbuds created by Nothing, designed with a multitude of sophisticated features catering to diverse audio needs. Prominent features include Active Noise Cancellation (ANC), capable of reducing noise levels by up to 50dB, allowing for a customizable listening experience via the Nothing X App. These earbuds offer a dual connection mode, enabling seamless connectivity to multiple devices, with the capability for auto-reconnection under certain conditions. Users can enjoy various audio enhancements such as spatial audio effects and multiple equalizer presets. 

The CMF Buds Pro 2 are compatible with both Android and iOS devices, featuring robust protection against dust and sweat, making them suitable for diverse environments and activities. The design includes intuitive touch controls for easy management of music playback, volume adjustments, and ANC settings. However, some users have reported issues with rapid battery drain attributed to high volume settings and specific codec usage. Additionally, these earbuds support fast charging, ensuring minimal downtime between uses. Overall, the CMF Buds Pro 2 provide a comprehensive and adaptable audio experience enhanced by modern technological advancements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39d4901014b867cda8bfaf59458315b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbcfd0ba7e5f79063be82c76153444e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597495</data>
</node>
<node id="Nothing Ear (1)">
  <data key="d0">Nothing Ear (1)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nothing Ear (1) is a model of earbuds designed to optimize audio performance through configurations like AAC mode to enhance battery life and connectivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Nothing Ear (1) is a wireless earbud offering various features such as ANC modes, Bluetooth capabilities, and compatibility with the Nothing X app.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597495</data>
</node>
<node id="iOS App Store">
  <data key="d0">iOS App Store</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The iOS App Store is Apple's digital distribution platform designed for iOS devices, where users can download applications, games, and other content. Among the various apps available, the Nothing X App is offered for download on this platform. This app allows users to configure and manage features related to the Nothing Ear (open) and Buds, providing functionality for controlling their settings. The iOS App Store facilitates the downloading and updating of the Nothing X App for users seeking to enhance their audio experience with Nothing devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597502</data>
</node>
<node id="AAC Mode">
  <data key="d0">AAC Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AAC Mode refers to an audio codec setting available on Nothing Ear earbuds that can improve battery performance during audio playback.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597502</data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth Device">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth Device</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Bluetooth Device is a technical term referencing smartphones, tablets, or laptops that can connect wirelessly to Nothing earphones for audio streaming.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5712d3b2c04697652ebea3ad203a5e64</data>
