</node>
<node id="App Store">
  <data key="d0">App Store</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The App Store is Apple's digital distribution platform specifically designed for iOS devices, serving as an online service where users can download a variety of applications. Among the apps available for download are the Nothing X app and the CMF Watch app. This service facilitates iOS users in accessing a plethora of applications, ensuring seamless integration and functionality with their devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-852b3a0efad903b6a432ebd5e7a404af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f73d28d893bcd51ecb5c4b3b1f54870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4524a05ac17de1be9923e9a9dc9c59</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597531</data>
</node>
<node id="Voice Assistant">
  <data key="d0">Voice Assistant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Voice Assistant is a versatile digital assistant feature that can be activated and controlled through the Nothing X app. It is designed to enhance user interaction with various devices, such as the Nothing Ear (open), CMF earbuds, and CMF Buds Pro 2, by facilitating voice commands for hands-free operation. Users can engage with the Voice Assistant via gestures set in the app, allowing seamless access to virtual assistant functions on devices like Ear (a) and Buds. This feature provides users with the convenience and efficiency of interacting with their devices through simple voice commands, enhancing the overall user experience without the need for manual control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597533</data>
</node>
<node id="LDAC">
  <data key="d0">LDAC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">LDAC is a high-definition audio codec supported by Ear (2) that allows streaming of high-resolution audio at high transmission bit rates.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC is a high-definition audio codec supported by Ear (a), enabling high-resolution audio streaming at 990kbps.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC is a high-definition audio codec used for improving audio quality over Bluetooth connections.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC is an audio codec provided by Nothing Ear, known for transmitting high-resolution audio.&lt;SEP&gt;LDAC is an audio coding technology allowing high-resolution audio transmission over Bluetooth, enhancing sound quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597533</data>
</node>
<node id="Gesture Controls">
  <data key="d0">Gesture Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">Gesture Controls allow users to manage audio playback, call handling, and other functions on the Ear (2) earbuds.&lt;SEP&gt;Gesture Controls refer to the touch-based operations on CMF Earbuds that allow users to play/pause audio, control calls, and activate other features through gestures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca8764057d5d820c4c3fb502a440d2f</data>
