<node id="AAC">
  <data key="d0">AAC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AAC is a Bluetooth codec supported by Ear (a), used commonly across various devices for audio transmission.&lt;SEP&gt;AAC is an audio codec supported by iOS devices for high-quality audio streaming over Bluetooth.&lt;SEP&gt;AAC is an audio coding format that provides high-quality digital audio sound, supported by the earbuds.&lt;SEP&gt;AAC is an audio format supported by Nothing Ear, ensuring compatibility with a wide range of devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9</data>
