<node id="Active Noise Cancellation">
  <data key="d0">Active Noise Cancellation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature that reduces unwanted ambient sounds using active noise control on the CMF Buds Pro 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation is a feature in Buds Pro that reduces ambient sound, enhancing the listening experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation is a mode on Ear (a) that reduces ambient noise for clearer listening.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation is a mode on the Buds that minimizes ambient noise for an enhanced audio experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597533</data>
</node>
<node id="Transparency Mode">
  <data key="d0">Transparency Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Transparency Mode is a feature found in various audio devices, such as Ear (a), Neckband Pro, Buds, and CMF Buds Pro 2. This feature enhances user awareness of their surroundings by allowing ambient sounds to be heard alongside audio playback. It simulates the effect of not wearing earbuds, enabling users to maintain situational awareness while listening to audio. Transparency Mode provides the ability to hear external sounds, making it particularly useful for maintaining awareness in different environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56220d4c1145af0000fc9cb728dc6db7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597536</data>
</node>
<node id="Touch Controls">
  <data key="d0">Touch Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Touch Controls are interactive features on CMF Buds Pro 2, allowing users to manage playback, calls, and other settings with finger gestures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8b23107caad65d85305805a37ddbe28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597536</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF">
  <data key="d0">CMF</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF is the organization that produces the CMF Buds Pro 2 and provides customer support for its products.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597536</data>
</node>
<node id="Spatial Audio Effect">
  <data key="d0">Spatial Audio Effect</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Spatial Audio Effect enhances audio experience by utilizing the Head-Related Transfer Function model.&lt;SEP&gt;Spatial Audio Effect in CMF Buds Pro 2 uses the Head-Related Transfer Function model to create a 3D immersive sound experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Spatial Audio Effect is a feature in the Neckband Pro that creates an immersive 3D sound experience using the HRTF model.&lt;SEP&gt;Spatial Audio Effect is a feature providing a 3D cinematic-grade sound experience based on the Head-Related Transfer Function model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597536</data>
</node>
<node id="Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF)">
  <data key="d0">Head-Related Transfer Function (HRTF)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">HRTF is a model used in audio engineering to emulate how sound reaches the ear from different points in space, aiding in the creation of spatial audio effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-310bcdfd35de1b898e48e8659f40d35e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597536</data>
</node>
<node id="Smart ANC Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Smart ANC Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Smart ANC Algorithm is an advanced noise cancellation technology that adjusts parameters based on environmental noise levels to optimize user experience.&lt;SEP&gt;The Smart ANC Algorithm is used by Ear (a) to provide adaptive active noise cancellation depending on the environmental noise level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597536</data>
</node>
<node id="Plastic Casing">
  <data key="d0">Plastic Casing</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">High-quality plastic casing is used in CMF Buds Pro 2 for durability, UV resistance, and impact resistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597536</data>
</node>
<node id="Silicone Ear Tips">
  <data key="d0">Silicone Ear Tips</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Silicone ear tips are designed for comfortable and secure fitting in the CMF Buds Pro 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicone ear tips enhance the comfort and fit of Ear (a) earbuds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597536</data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth 5.3">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth 5.3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth 5.3 is a wireless technology standard that facilitates efficient and seamless connectivity between devices. This version of Bluetooth technology is utilized by various products, including Ear (a), Nothing Ear, Watch Pro, Buds Pro, Buds, CMF Buds Pro 2, and Neckband Pro. Each of these devices benefits from the improved connectivity and performance offered by Bluetooth 5.3, enhancing their ability to communicate wirelessly with other devices. This version is particularly noted for its advanced capabilities in maintaining strong, stable connections across multiple device interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c923c17927fa4e291cc287467061e0cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597538</data>
</node>
<node id="IP55 Protection Rating">
  <data key="d0">IP55 Protection Rating</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">IP55 Rating means that CMF Buds Pro 2 are level 5 dustproof and level 5 waterproof, offering resistance to dust and water.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597538</data>
</node>
<node id="DIRAC OPTEO">
  <data key="d0">DIRAC OPTEO</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">DIRAC OPTEO is one of the equalizer presets available for CMF Buds Pro 2, providing high-quality audio adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597538</data>
</node>
<node id="LDAC, AAC, SBC">
  <data key="d0">LDAC, AAC, SBC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">LDAC, AAC, and SBC are audio formats supported by CMF Buds Pro 2, offering varied audio quality parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-242b40fbdd789fce17cd5d53222cb91d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597538</data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Dial">
  <data key="d0">Smart Dial</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Smart Dial is a customizable control feature on the charging case that supports various functions such as volume control and noise cancellation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Smart Dial is a control mechanism on the Neckband Pro, allowing for various actions such as adjusting volume, switching noise cancellation modes, and controlling music playback.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597538</data>
</node>
<node id="Ultra Bass Technology">
  <data key="d0">Ultra Bass Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ultra Bass Technology enhances low-frequency signals in music for a more dynamic bass experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra Bass Technology enhances low-frequency sounds in real-time, providing dynamic audio enhancement for the Buds Pro earbuds.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra Bass Technology in the Buds enhances low-frequency signals dynamically, providing an enhanced bass experience adjustable through the Nothing X app.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultra Bass Technology is a sound enhancement feature in the Neckband Pro that improves the perception of low-frequency signals in music.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597538</data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptive Mode">
  <data key="d0">Adaptive Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adaptive Mode in Ear (a) adjusts noise cancellation levels based on environmental noise.&lt;SEP&gt;Adaptive Mode is a noise control feature that adjusts noise cancellation based on environmental sound levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597538</data>
</node>
<node id="Active Noise Cancellation (ANC)">
  <data key="d0">Active Noise Cancellation (ANC)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ANC is a technology used in Nothing Ear that reduces unwanted ambient sounds using active noise control.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature of CMF Buds 2 supporting noise reduction up to 48dB, enhancing user listening experience by eliminating ambient sounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation is a feature in earbuds designed to reduce unwanted ambient sounds using active noise control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7514c9c486c31232321ac43b9689ae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597538</data>
</node>
<node id="Dual Connection">
  <data key="d0">Dual Connection</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual Connection is a versatile feature available in various Nothing Ear earbuds, including models such as Ear (open), Ear (a), and Ear (2). This functionality allows the earbuds to connect simultaneously to two Bluetooth devices, enabling seamless management of audio playback and call audio priorities based on user activity. The feature enhances flexibility by allowing easy switching between devices and managing calls and audio playback seamlessly. Some earbuds, like CMF Buds 2, also support this feature, giving users the ability to connect to two different devices simultaneously, although users may occasionally experience sound output delays. Overall, Dual Connection provides users with the capability to stay connected across multiple devices, ensuring convenience and efficiency in handling audio functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e908dc520371478d52528beaf43780b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26891fa7fbcc5e292dab7ce65ee89518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1887c3e753e5f27cc1105a32465893f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c10ba86f3c652add8c1d23db1a9625b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597544</data>
</node>
<node id="Fast Charging">
  <data key="d0">Fast Charging</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Fast Charging capability of Nothing Ear (open) allows the earbuds to power up quickly, offering extended use with a short charging time.&lt;SEP&gt;Fast Charging in Ear (2) allows rapid power restore, enabling significant usage time after a short charge period.&lt;SEP&gt;Fast Charging is a feature available in CMF Buds 2, enabling quick recharge to provide extended usage time, notably providing 4-hour usage with a 10-minute charge without ANC.&lt;SEP&gt;Fast Charging is a feature of Ear (a) allowing quick charging, enabling extended usage with short charging durations.&lt;SEP&gt;Fast Charging is a feature of the Buds Pro Earbuds, allowing for quick recharge, providing 3 hours of use with a 10-minute charge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a8564fc99ee9391246494d993bc4be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbeb4732200e7559b14badeb7c65f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbdc3aa884ec77acb84402d00879691d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597544</data>
</node>
<node id="CMF Buds 2">
  <data key="d0">CMF Buds 2</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF Buds 2 are wireless earbuds offering features like Active Noise Cancellation, Spatial Audio Effect, and dual device connection, made with durable materials such as a high-quality plastic casing and silicone ear tips.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597544</data>
</node>
<node id="Dirac Opteo">
  <data key="d0">Dirac Opteo</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dirac Opteo is a default audio tuning option provided by the collaboration between CMF by Nothing and Dirac.&lt;SEP&gt;Dirac Opteo is a sound enhancement technology incorporated in the Buds to optimize audio output and maximize acoustic performance using patented correction technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Dirac Opteo is a sound optimization technology used in CMF Buds 2 for enhancing audio output by correcting sound resonances and colorations digitally.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597544</data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth 5.4">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth 5.4</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth 5.4 is the wireless technology standard used by CMF Buds 2 for connectivity with devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597544</data>
</node>
<node id="Google Fast Pair">
  <data key="d0">Google Fast Pair</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Google Fast Pair is a Bluetooth technology feature designed for quick and seamless pairing with compatible devices, especially Android devices. It is supported by several earbud models including CMF Buds 2, Buds Pro, Ear (2), Nothing Ear devices, Buds, Neckband Pro, and Ear (a). The feature facilitates a fast and easy setup process, enhancing the user experience by quickly connecting the earbuds to the desired devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597554</data>
</node>
<node id="Microsoft Swift Pair">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Swift Pair</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Swift Pair is a Bluetooth pairing technology designed to facilitate quick and seamless connections with compatible devices, particularly Windows PCs. It is supported by a variety of audio devices, including CMF Buds 2, Buds Pro, Ear (a), Neckband Pro, Ear (2), and Nothing Ear earbuds. This feature provides users with the convenience of streamlined and efficient pairing, enhancing the overall usability and connectivity experience with Windows systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9c603ca72c28f9a9a34c1ddfef9b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Android 6.0 and above">
  <data key="d0">Android 6.0 and above</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF Buds 2 are compatible with Android operating systems version 6.0 and above.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="iOS 13 and above">
  <data key="d0">iOS 13 and above</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">CMF Buds 2 are compatible with iOS operating systems version 13 and above.&lt;SEP&gt;Nothing Ear devices are compatible with iOS 13 and later versions, ensuring usage across various Apple devices.&lt;SEP&gt;iOS 13 and above are the Apple operating system versions compatible with the Watch Pro.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6dc70b538423eed2a153e23decae4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e27c35cbd2d81e7710bdeb957abdb9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="AAC and SBC">
  <data key="d0">AAC and SBC</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">AAC and SBC are audio codecs supported by CMF Buds 2 for optimal audio streaming.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Neckband Pro">
  <data key="d0">Neckband Pro</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Neckband Pro is a product featuring dual-connectivity, gesture control, volume adjustment, and noise cancellation modes.&lt;SEP&gt;Neckband Pro is a type of earphone that supports a variety of features including Ultra Bass technology, ANC, and various audio formats.&lt;SEP&gt;Neckband Pro is a type of wireless earphones mentioned in the context of call handling when connected to multiple devices.&lt;SEP&gt;The Neckband Pro is a model of earphones with advanced battery and playback features, not supporting wireless charging.&lt;SEP&gt;The Neckband Pro is a type of earphone with features such as waterproofing based on IEC 60529 standards, dual connectivity support via the Nothing X app, a battery capacity of 220mAh, and fast charging capability. It does not support wireless charging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93607977c7e870361284500bad913d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f8202293fdace1a3a66be97a3995370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a5e79a49bc7db2a612f28136aee41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbad053247bfe41ce192c651034259c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Buds">
  <data key="d0">Buds</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Buds are Bluetooth earphones that feature functions like dual connectivity, noise cancellation, and gesture controls.&lt;SEP&gt;The Buds are earphones featuring multiple functionalities such as ANC, Ultra Bass Technology, Dirac Opteo sound enhancement, and compatibility with Android and iOS systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth Earphones">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth Earphones</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth earphones are wireless audio devices that connect through Bluetooth technology, exemplified by the Buds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Noise Cancellation">
  <data key="d0">Noise Cancellation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Noise Cancellation in Ear (2) reduces ambient sounds to enhance the listening experience, with customizable modes available.&lt;SEP&gt;Noise Cancellation is a feature in the Buds to reduce ambient sound, offering Active Noise Cancellation and Transparency Mode.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-716596cbb2a7e8b3702d6ceb7f52724e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebeef135007ca56eca4d845a2c04e9d0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Buds Pro">
  <data key="d0">Buds Pro</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">The Buds Pro are high-tech earbuds featuring touch controls, customizable features via the Nothing X app, Ultra Bass Technology, and support for various audio formats, including AAC and SBC. They offer functionalities like Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC) and can connect up to eight devices. Compatibility includes Android 5.1 and iOS 13 and above, and they support Google Fast Pair and Microsoft Swift Pair.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC)">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Noise Cancellation (ENC)</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">ENC is a feature designed to minimize unwanted background noise during calls or when using the earbuds' microphone.&lt;SEP&gt;ENC is a noise-cancelling technology that reduces background noise during microphone usage for calls.&lt;SEP&gt;ENC is a technology integrated into the Buds Pro to reduce unwanted background noise during calls, ensuring clear communication.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Noise Cancellation is a feature similar to Active Noise Cancellation, specifically tuned to remove unwanted background noise during calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1bc8f3ce2d2c5d835ffeade41737ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026c9aac607d8ab10d1f5ae9d51556e9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Polycarbonate Plastic">
  <data key="d0">Polycarbonate Plastic</data>
  <data key="d1">material</data>
  <data key="d2">Polycarbonate Plastic is used in the construction of the Buds Pro, known for its UV resistance and impact resistance properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c721c853ee8f8f0dc302ae4d23208b8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="Buds Pro Earbuds">
  <data key="d0">Buds Pro Earbuds</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Buds Pro Earbuds are in-ear wireless devices offering features like active noise cancellation, IP54 dustproof and waterproof rating, and fast charging capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597569</data>
</node>
<node id="ANC">
  <data key="d0">ANC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ANC stands for Active Noise Cancellation, a feature in the Buds allowing for reduction of ambient sounds during use.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature of Buds Pro earbuds reducing noise up to 45 dB.&lt;SEP&gt;Active Noise Cancellation (ANC) is a feature that reduces ambient sounds, enhancing listening experiences in the Neckband Pro.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8464f2a22c355940190a72202a4bd5a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8e8ce97e9623a3206989beb9bb64519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb83fc961a06d6a2e205ffa27cd9700</data>
