  <data key="d2">App Locker is a feature for securing apps with passwords, fingerprints, or facial recognition in Nothing OS 2.0.0.&lt;SEP&gt;App Locker is a feature that allows users to lock specific apps to protect personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;App Locker is a security feature that allows users to lock specific apps to protect their personal data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34426e6693364728fe244fbfe87a0629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b51e206cee412c86265f35f8120e9d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597608</data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Share">
  <data key="d0">Battery Share</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery Share allows users to wirelessly share their phone's battery with other devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Battery Share is a feature allowing the Nothing Phone to share its battery power with other devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Battery Share is a feature that allows one device to charge another, available on Phone (1).&lt;SEP&gt;Battery Share is a feature that is not supported on certain devices but commonly allows sharing battery power between devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a79d8dc4ced2f49b73dd01d066a09896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63b51e206cee412c86265f35f8120e9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597608</data>
</node>
<node id="Glyph Interface">
  <data key="d0">Glyph Interface</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Glyph Interface is a distinctive and customizable feature prominently found on the Nothing Phone, incorporating light strips on the back of the device. This innovative interface is designed to enhance user interaction and communication through unique visual patterns, sound, and vibration. Users can personalize their experience by adjusting ringtones, notifications, brightness, and styles. Additionally, the Glyph Interface offers a Bedtime Schedule to disable phone notifications at specific times, further refining its user-centric capabilities. It provides visual feedback when Google Assistant is activated and supports light-only alerts, allowing users to set their phones to silent mode if desired. This feature, often managed through the device's settings, enables a user to enable or disable Glyph lights and select various patterns for notifications and ringtones. As an iconic element of the Nothing Phone, the Glyph Interface represents a novel method of communication and interaction, setting it apart as a unique design aspect yet not supported by Google Assistant directly.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d629090523155bf0dd12f9021e8a28a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34426e6693364728fe244fbfe87a0629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcde7317fc7b036415d89ea81329b232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281d19d9c4f252fd5c844c3d467ca398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41ebb68d062de192afe8e06b1a67a1c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9ca0a66c298c31fec04cbfc30d7b98c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b7b5b1eb951ce536bdbb599b623332a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d866982ab2e7ced6661f8a940789dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d9ff89b42c8123f60ebe4521bfb0cbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1bc17eaf113f533442b214ae6b6dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9025d462a4f9ed5f5840d5850b11449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d52fb5275de8c3b54cbe38e612348505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c14c96115117369f38094721a77a31ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af070275f346cb3aabc6679c7791a2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36249177cb5d5f7c720a6f64a0edc813&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4524a05ac17de1be9923e9a9dc9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77d37b7781a21f9ace596c3bcb0cbfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0028e301a1da668320afc0e2e78601b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27081652ef7a553b2a6096008ef80269</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1767597611</data>
</node>
