<node id="MMS">
  <data key="d0">MMS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending images and other media content over data networks or WiFi.&lt;SEP&gt;MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is a standard way to send messages that include multimedia content, like images, over a cellular network.&lt;SEP&gt;MMS allows sending images via the SMS app using a data network or WiFi connection.&lt;SEP&gt;MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, enabling the sending of images and other multimedia over a data network.&lt;SEP&gt;MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, used to send multi-media messages such as images.</data>
